3.6 Host monitoring gaps

Visual: Table. This lists hosts tagged to a Claims app that sent no data in 24 hours, or that went stale in the last 15 minutes. from:-7d on the entity fetch keeps recently disappeared hosts in the list.

fetch dt.entity.host, from:-7d
| fields id, hostName = entity.name, tags
| expand tag = tags
| filter startsWith(tag, "APMID:")
| fieldsAdd apmid = splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1]
| filter in(apmid, array($ClaimsApps))
| lookup [
    timeseries cpu = avg(dt.host.cpu.usage), by:{dt.entity.host}, from:-24h, interval:5m
    | fieldsAdd seen24h = arraySize(arrayRemoveNulls(cpu)) > 0,
                seen15m = arraySize(arrayRemoveNulls(arraySlice(cpu, from:-3))) > 0
    | fields dt.entity.host, seen24h, seen15m
  ], sourceField: id, lookupField: dt.entity.host, prefix: "m."
| fieldsAdd gap = if(not(coalesce(m.seen24h, false)), "No data in 24h",
                  else: if(not(coalesce(m.seen15m, false)), "Stale (>15 min)", else: "OK"))
| filter gap != "OK"
| fields apmid, hostName, gap
| sort gap asc, apmid asc


Hosts that are "No data in 24h" are probably decommissioned hosts that still carry the tag. They're worth sending to the CMDB team as cleanup.

